Good.

1079
00:45:45,400 --> 00:45:45,719
Good.

1080
00:45:46,260 --> 00:45:46,579
OK.

1081
00:45:48,800 --> 00:45:49,440
In 2020.

1082
00:45:49,440 --> 00:45:49,800
In 2020.

1083
00:45:49,800 --> 00:45:51,980
2012, you must understand, there was nothing more

1084
00:45:51,980 --> 00:45:53,679
that I cared about in my career as a magician.

1085
00:45:54,440 --> 00:45:55,980
Professionally, in my industry, this

1086
00:45:55,980 --> 00:45:57,179
was the most impossible thing.

1087
00:45:57,400 --> 00:45:59,780
And all I had to work with was four sentences

1088
00:45:59,780 --> 00:46:03,699
from a newspaper extract from 1907 that described this trick.

1089
00:46:03,940 --> 00:46:05,860
So I took that extract, I photocopied it

1090
00:46:05,860 --> 00:46:08,119
from my state library, took it to all my magic buddies

1091
00:46:08,119 --> 00:46:09,579
and said, we must learn this.

1092
00:46:09,940 --> 00:46:12,079
This is the most impossible thing to do in our industry.

1093
00:46:12,920 --> 00:46:16,000
And they all looked at me and they said, far out, mate.

1094
00:46:16,039 --> 00:46:16,420
Calm down.

1095
00:46:18,750 --> 00:46:21,389
Then a book like that has 100,000 words.

1096
00:46:21,389 --> 00:46:23,389
That's 100,000 out of one.

1097
00:46:25,610 --> 00:46:26,170
It's impossible.

1098
00:46:26,750 --> 00:46:27,590
You're an idiot.

1099
