Obviously, I removed them from my top five.

1100
00:46:34,710 --> 00:46:37,389
And something truly profound came as a result.

1101
00:46:38,150 --> 00:46:40,610
All my magic buddies who believed that this could not

1102
00:46:40,610 --> 00:46:41,949
be done, guess what?

1103
00:46:42,710 --> 00:46:45,050
They didn't even try.

1104
00:46:46,630 --> 00:46:47,829
They didn't even try.

1105
00:46:48,489 --> 00:46:49,190
And guess what?

1106
00:46:49,210 --> 00:46:49,969
When they tried?

1107
00:46:50,030 --> 00:46:50,929
When they tried?

1108
00:46:50,929 --> 00:46:52,489
They half-arsed it.

1109
00:46:53,050 --> 00:46:56,670
They didn't even give it a full arse, right?

1110
00:46:57,929 --> 00:46:58,250
Yeah.

1111
00:47:01,980 --> 00:47:05,400
I gave this both cheeks, OK?

1112
00:47:06,320 --> 00:47:07,559
And here's the thing.

1113
00:47:08,199 --> 00:47:09,659
I found the method.

1114
00:47:10,059 --> 00:47:11,780
I discovered the method.

1115
00:47:12,619 --> 00:47:14,780
And my friends, moving forward in life professionally

1116
00:47:14,780 --> 00:47:18,019
and personally, you will face challenges that feel impossible.

1117
00:47:18,420 --> 00:47:20,980
You will want to have goals that sometimes feel

1118
00:47:20,980 --> 00:47:21,980
outrageous and impossible.

1119
00:47:21,980 --> 00:47:24,079
I want to tell you how this trick is done.

1120
00:47:24,400 --> 00:47:25,300
I'm going to teach you.

1121
00:47:26,219 --> 00:47:28,260
Because I know you will face these impossible challenges

1122
00:47:28,260 --> 00:47:29,880
and impossible goals that you want to achieve.

1123
00:47:30,320 --> 00:47:32,860
So let me tell you how magicians create the impossible.

1124
00:47:33,360 --> 00:47:35,539
And use this as a metaphor the next time you encounter

1125
00:47:35,539 --> 00:47:37,539
something that seems challenging or difficult.

1126
00:47:38,099 --> 00:47:40,039
You see, what's the first step?

1127
00:47:40,500 --> 00:47:42,739
What's the first step to creating the impossible?

1128
00:47:43,019 --> 00:47:44,039
So that's my question to you.

1129
00:47:44,079 --> 00:47:45,019
What is that first step?

1130
00:47:45,059 --> 00:47:45,460
What is it?

1131
00:47:46,239 --> 00:47:51,960
The first step is, you must fundamentally believe with conviction that it can be done.

1132
00:47:51,980 --> 00:47:55,400
But why is this belief thing so important?

1133
00:47:55,559 --> 00:47:55,760
Why?

1134
00:47:56,440 --> 00:48:00,940
This belief thing is important because your beliefs dictate your actions in life.

1135
00:48:01,239 --> 00:48:03,760
Your beliefs dictate your actions.

1136
00:48:04,079 --> 00:48:06,699
So when you believe something can be done with conviction,

1137
00:48:06,900 --> 00:48:09,139
it dictates your actions and you take the first step.

1138
00:48:09,380 --> 00:48:12,820
And only when you take the first step can you see step two.

1139
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:15,420
You cannot see step two from step zero.

1140
00:48:15,559 --> 00:48:16,960
You've got to be on step one.

1141
00:48:17,840 --> 00:48:20,480
What's the first instruction I gave Joshua?

1142
00:48:20,619 --> 00:48:21,260
Do you remember?

1143
00:48:22,139 --> 00:48:24,940
I said, open the book to a random page.

1144
00:48:25,099 --> 00:48:26,820
And I really said random, random, random.

1145
00:48:26,920 --> 00:48:28,480
Even to the point he was like, random.

1146
00:48:29,400 --> 00:48:29,800
Right?

1147
00:48:30,219 --> 00:48:31,940
And what did he do when he said that?

1148
00:48:32,039 --> 00:48:33,760
He went somewhere in the middle.

1149
00:48:34,840 --> 00:48:37,559
Because random feels like it's in the middle.

1150
00:48:37,880 --> 00:48:39,639
You tell anybody in the Western countries,

1151
00:48:39,780 --> 00:48:43,019
random, nobody goes for the first 25% or the last 25%.

1152
00:48:43,019 --> 00:48:45,980
People always go for the middle 50%.

1153
00:48:45,980 --> 00:48:47,539
Because that feels random.

1154
00:48:48,440 --> 00:48:50,219
So just like that, you take the second step.

1155
00:48:50,219 --> 00:48:52,539
It's not one out of 100,000.

1156
00:48:52,780 --> 00:48:54,619
It's one out of 50,000.

1157
00:48:54,960 --> 00:48:56,219
It's a lot easier, right?

1158
00:48:57,500 --> 00:48:57,860
No.

1159
00:48:59,079 --> 00:48:59,820
No, it's not.

1160
00:49:00,559 --> 00:49:02,239
You lose your mind on step two.

1161
00:49:02,340 --> 00:49:04,280
You dye your hair blonde and you go crazy.

1162
00:49:05,320 --> 00:49:05,679
Yeah.

1163
00:49:06,280 --> 00:49:07,599
But why do you keep going though?

1164
00:49:07,639 --> 00:49:08,300
You must think about this.

1165
00:49:08,360 --> 00:49:09,519
Why do you keep going?

1166
00:49:09,639 --> 00:49:12,900
Why do entrepreneurs or why do magicians keep going in the face of adversity

1167
00:49:12,900 --> 00:49:14,739
or when the odds are stacked against them?

1168
00:49:14,800 --> 00:49:15,320
Why do you keep going?

1169
00:49:16,300 --> 00:49:17,800
Because you believe it can be done.

1170
00:49:18,619 --> 00:49:20,260
Because you believe there's a way.

1171
00:49:20,760 --> 00:49:21,980
So you stay on track.

1172
00:49:22,219 --> 00:49:24,219
You don't fall victim to asylum mentality.

1173
00:49:24,559 --> 00:49:27,800
You ask for a perspective you've never collaborated with before.

1174
00:49:28,039 --> 00:49:29,760
So you ask a linguist.

1175
00:49:30,039 --> 00:49:31,619
Never talked to a linguist before.

1176
00:49:32,099 --> 00:49:32,900
Different perspective.

1177
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:35,000
And I said, what's the next step, Miss Linguist?

1178
00:49:35,380 --> 00:49:37,400
And she goes, oh, Vin, the next step is so simple.

1179
00:49:37,420 --> 00:49:38,019
You are an idiot.

1180
00:49:39,019 --> 00:49:41,820
Just ask them to pick a long word, not a short word.

1181
00:49:42,420 --> 00:49:44,280
And then she told me, do you know what that means, Vin?

1182
00:49:44,380 --> 00:49:46,599
A long word is a word with more than six letters.

1183
00:49:47,239 --> 00:49:51,900
Because anything with less than six letters looks visually short next to the long words.

1184
00:49:52,260 --> 00:49:55,920
So if you remove every single word in the middle 50% that has less than six letters,

1185
00:49:56,460 --> 00:49:58,679
you've now removed more than 90% of this.

1186
00:49:59,539 --> 00:50:00,739
So you take the next step.

1187
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:02,320
It's not one out of 50,000.

1188
00:50:02,860 --> 00:50:05,179
It's one out of 5,000.

1189
00:50:05,519 --> 00:50:08,679
And the next two steps will blow your minds as to how this is done.

1190
00:50:10,360 --> 00:50:11,539
But I'm not sharing it.

1191
00:50:12,119 --> 00:50:12,519
No.

1192
00:50:14,239 --> 00:50:16,199
Because how this trick is done is not important to you.

1193
00:50:16,260 --> 00:50:16,579
You're not moving.

1194
00:50:16,599 --> 00:50:17,039
You're not magicians.

1195
00:50:17,300 --> 00:50:19,639
But the most important thing, my friends, is this first step.

1196
00:50:20,219 --> 00:50:23,760
Far too often when we look at the goals or the challenges that we face moving forward,

1197
00:50:23,880 --> 00:50:29,059
far too often we give the challenge or the difficult goal, we go, oh, it's impossible.

1198
00:50:29,500 --> 00:50:30,519
I can't do this.

1199
00:50:30,820 --> 00:50:32,199
And you don't even try.

1200
00:50:33,800 --> 00:50:39,260
So I'm going to prove to you that anything can be achieved, that anything is possible.

1201
00:50:39,800 --> 00:50:45,239
But before I do this, if any of you want any of my other talks, if you want a copy of this talk,

1202
00:50:45,239 --> 00:50:49,539
or if you want my keynote slides, or you'd like to join me for a workshop at some point in Long Beach,

1203
